body:
After some second thoughts, why not restrict the scope of this function to only the `items` provided prop as it will be for now only used when filtering or sorting `items`.

The api will become:

we had a prop called `transformItems`. It will take the `items` as a parameter, and expect in return the same `items` structure.
This props, if exists, will be called each time a connector called its `getProvidedProps` function.
Will only be available on widgets that have an `items` provided props.

ex of usage:

```js
<RefinementList attributeName="category" 	
				transformItems={items => {
      				return orderBy(items, ['label'], ['asc']);
				}}
/>
```
